{"meta":{"status":true,"timestamp":1779448336,"versions":{"requested":"v2025.1.LTS","mapped":"v2.228","concrete":"v2.228.25"},"records":1},"data":[{"id":"0157_luser-559b39a3-4979-518d-a846-4c3668af1149_f208e070-82fe-5809-bd07-ebaf663d8b41_ba4355d7b6ba0f8ad2239383989b18f2","user_id":"luser-559b39a3-4979-518d-a846-4c3668af1149","response_id":"f208e070-82fe-5809-bd07-ebaf663d8b41_ba4355d7b6ba0f8ad2239383989b18f2","type":"longtextV2","question":{"type":"longtextV2","options":null,"metadata":{"source":{"organisation_id":154},"sheet_reference":"0486c0c5-e66e-52c3-8ba6-63c6fa038ef9","widget_reference":"0486c0c5-e66e-52c3-8ba6-63c6fa038ef9_question","valid_response_count":0},"stimulus":"<p><img height=\"1126\" src=\"https://assets.learnosity.com/organisations/154/e6e1d990-b875-4b4f-84b1-af4647161494.jpg\" width=\"1559\"></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>Answer the following questions based on the population pyramids shown above:&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>1. How has the population composition changed from 1940 to 2020? (This is a compare question - you MUST discuss BOTH pyramids and the changes that occurred to receive full credit).&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>2. Given this trend, what do you&nbsp;<strong><em>predict&nbsp;</em></strong>the population composition of the United States will be in 2050? Explain your reasoning. (This is an EXPLAIN question - you must provide a prediction and then tell your reader why you think that will happen).&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>3. What possible events could alter this trend? Explain your reasoning. (Again, this is an EXPLAIN question, so identify an event that might alter the pattern, and then tell your reader how the trend would change).&nbsp;</p>\n","response_id":"f208e070-82fe-5809-bd07-ebaf663d8b41_ba4355d7b6ba0f8ad2239383989b18f2"},"response":{"value":"<p>From 1940 to 2018, the population pyramid's composition has changed to now there is a more stable growth instead of the relatively high population growth. In 1940 the US was in stage 3 of DTM which population pyramid wise, we were more in a triangle shape instead of a box because of the fact there are many more children because there was less urbanization and the socially status of women was not as high as it is today and it was culturally expected. Also there was more of a need to have more children back then rather than there is right now. This is a sign of the population going up. Now we are in stage 5 after going through decades of one generation having less kids than their own generation because the need of having more children has lessened. Slowly this led to the healthy population pyramid there is today.</p><p>In the future there is going to be a population decline for the USA because our replacement rate is less than 2.1. This can lead to an economic crisis if this trend intensifies as there won't be enough people to do the essential needs of the country. The rate in our country is acceptable but in countries like South Korea they are predicted to lose 2/3 of their population! This can be a huge disaster. if the replacement rate doesn't improve.</p><p>Events that could alter this trend are wars or economic crises as both would lead to reasons why not to have any kids and the population decline would be much steeper than it is even right now. Historically it has been shown that when one of these events happens, the fertility rate drops by a lot. This makes sense because these are testing times when couples are thinking about their future and wondering about the fact if they can afford to have a child or not.</p><p><br></p>","wordCount":318,"type":"string","apiVersion":"v2.197.34","revision":21},"creation_date":"2025-09-10 16:44:26","mod_date":"2025-09-10 17:07:28","persist_until":"2028-09-09 16:44:26","saved":true}]}